==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 1~5 seconds<sup>30f~150f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>, delay 3~7 seconds<sup>90f~210f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 2~9 seconds<sup>60f~270f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 45~50 seconds<sup>1,350f~1,500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 85% HP:
**Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 35~40 seconds<sup>1,050f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Heavy Assault C.A.T. (Enemy)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Heavy Assault C.A.T. is outranged by [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] but will be able to hit almost everything closer, so spam plenty of meatshields to keep Bahamut safe from the Dark enemies while you chip away at the boss. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] also helps greatly in managing the wave of enemies and keeping them pinned at the base. Use [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cats]] to keep the enemies away from Bahamut (and Ururun if you brought her) when he's not attacking.

[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] can easily handle the never-ending [[Croco]]s with its [[Wave Attack]]s. You can spawn a few meatshields and a [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Cooldown Cat]] early on in the stage to max your wallet, but don't send in too many cats or you'll summon the boss before you're ready.

If you have any [[Long Distance]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] or [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]], you can keep the enemies pinned at their base and your units can destroy the base before you kill the boss.

